description:
RFC-078 (Valence rfc-j5f) ACCEPTED 2026-10-01 (comment 01:32) under RFC-056's duty model, with RFC-075 (spoke duties) and RFC-076 (join/declaration) accepted the same night.

The accessory profile = a hub with a minimal duty set, which the generated Isotope firmware must meet:
- parser totality (every malformed frame refused, never a crash);
- declaration-as-catalog: the accessory's own section 8.1 catalog served over blob namespace 0, verified by etag, every field carrying its REQUIRED safe value, at most 30 own channels (RFC-076 slice r=2..31), no STORE entries, group strings are the accessory's own;
- INTENT/ECHO for actuators; STATE pushed without SUBSCRIBE; the registered accessory-status entry at relative 0x01;
- RFC-075 spoke duties: active scan on channels 1-13, beacon-only deadman (5 s, GOODBYE, or any ESTOP = safe state now), every frame within 250 B, durable u64 accessory_id, window-free re-join with etag-match skip;
- interlock: commanded safe values from the hub (pause, ESTOP) applied immediately; nothing re-arms on its own.
Absent by profile: session layer, tiers, pairing, trust, arbitration, other bindings. Every wire number from the Valence generated registry, never local.

Waits on iso-3ph validations and the generator shape (DESIGN.md Q9).

Prove it: host test of the accessory core against a recorded hub session (declaration fetch, intent, deadman trip) exits 0; bench: deadman to safe state measured on a pin (iso-3ph.3 rig) within 5 s + one beacon; Valence conformance probe's accessory-profile step (once it exists) PASSes.
